{"event": "web_search", "data": {"request_id": "f3c9765c64e3", "seq": 11, "ts": "2026-10-27T16:58:05.732Z", "t_ms": 9297, "agent": "research", "tool": "tavily_search", "server": "tavily-remote-mcp", "transport": "streamable_http", "purpose": "find current developments on the topic", "query": "capital of Australia", "time_range": null, "status": "ok", "latency_ms": 3621, "results": [{"cite_id": "W1", "url": "https://ovolohotels.com/ovolo/blog/sydney-isnt-the-capital-of-australia", "title": "What's the Capital of Australia? Not Sydney or Melbourne! | Ovolo Blog", "domain": "ovolohotels.com", "score": 0.8758, "retrieved_at": "2026-10-27T16:58:02.110Z", "snippet": "Australia is one of those countries with a capital city that isn’t very well known or densely populated. Other examples of countries like this include Brazil with its capital Brasilia, Turkey with Ankara, and Switzerland with its capital city Bern. Foreigners often debate between"}, {"cite_id": "W2", "url": "https://youtooproject.com/en/blog/australia-en/capital-of-australia-canberra", "title": "What is the capital of Australia? If you thought it was Sydney, keep on reading", "domain": "youtooproject.com", "score": 0.873, "retrieved_at": "2026-10-27T16:58:02.110Z", "snippet": "If you are surprised to learn that this is not the case, maybe you will give Melbourne a try. Well, it’s not either! The capital of Australia is Canberra. Now, don’t just keep the answer for your next trivia game with your friends and discover the whole story.\n\n## The origin of A"}, {"cite_id": "W3", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra", "title": "Canberra - Wikipedia", "domain": "en.wikipedia.org", "score": 0.8528, "retrieved_at": "2026-10-27T16:58:02.110Z", "snippet": "Canberra (/ˈkænbrə/ ⓘ KAN-brə; Ngunawal: Kanbarra) is the capital city of Australia and the largest population centre in the Australian Capital Territory. With an estimated population of 484,630 as of 2025, Canberra is Australia's largest inland city and the eighth-largest Austra"}, {"cite_id": "W4", "url": "https://www.ebsco.com/research-starters/geography-and-cartography/canberra-australia", "title": "Canberra, Australia | Geography and Cartography | Research Starters | EBSCOhost", "domain": "www.ebsco.com", "score": 0.8316, "retrieved_at": "2026-10-27T16:58:02.110Z", "snippet": "Canberra, the capital of Australia and the Australian Capital Territory (ACT), is a uniquely planned city established to serve as the nation's administrative center. Developed after the ACT's formation in 1908, Canberra spans approximately 805.6 square kilometers (311 square mile"}]}, "client_ms": 9299}
